// and consumption only refuses the BRIDGE case:
//     if (bs.pending_view && bs.vcol_bridge) continue;
// So a slot with pending_view TRUE and vcol_bridge FALSE is consumed with a
// vcol taken from a publish up to 50 ms old - three frames at 67 fps - while
// its sm came from THIS frame's resolve. wpos -> view -> shadow UV is then
// offset by exactly that camera delta: offset not absent, proportional to
// motion, zero at rest, worst where the vz gradient across the box is largest
// (steep look-down), and transient because the next publish completes the
// seal. Every clause of the report, and bandProvSkips 0 says the guard that
// exists does not cover it.
// MEASURED FIRST. bandPendRuns against the flicker count is the field match;
// bandPendAgeMaxMs is how stale the vcol actually got.
//   bandPendRuns ~= what you see -> confirmed. The repair is to pair vcol
//       with the epoch sm came from instead of with whatever publish is
//       within 50 ms - the same correction 26172 made on the cast side.
//   bandPendRuns ~0 -> wrong again, and the 148 ms seal age is next.
static uint64_t g_band_pend_consumed = 0;   // cycles the winner had a provisional vcol
