// 26265 THE COMPOSITE ARMED ON EXISTENCE, NOT ON FRESHNESS.
//
// The injection arms on khv_eng_ok - the copy's own return value, this frame.
// Both composite sites armed on (g_svs_eng_cb != nullptr), and that buffer is
// created ONCE and lives until the device dies. So from the first successful
// copy onward the composite would arm on EVERY frame, including every frame
// where the copy SKIPPED because the latched resource was not bound
// (engCopySkips) - consuming a stale engine rotation while engArmComp read 1.
//
// A frame-late rotation is the precise defect this whole path exists to fix,
// so an arm that cannot tell fresh from stale would have re-created it inside
// the fix and reported success. One frame of slack is admitted deliberately -
// svVolAgeMax 1 already documents that shift between the injection and the
// late flush - and anything older is refused and counted.
